SUMMARY:[Geophysics Department] Geophysics Seminar - Emily Geyman\, "Learn
 ing from landscapes: The climate sensitivity of glaciers and the mechanics
  of soil production"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T130000
DTSTAMP:20261022T175237Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54001589975173-54001597749326@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Many processes shaping Earth’s surface unfold over timescale
 s that are too long to observe directly. I will present two vignettes illu
 strating how space-for-time substitution approaches allow us to leverage o
 bservations across space to constrain both rates and mechanisms of change 
 over time. In the Arctic Archipelago of Svalbard\, historical reconstructi
 ons of 1\,594 glaciers reveal how ice loss varies across climate gradients
 \, providing an empirical basis for quantifying the sensitivity of ice lo
 \n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-22 10:52 PDT
LOCATION:Mitchell Earth Sciences
END:VEVENT
